From cc8a59a6cb2bba0f2f3209ea8cdf125768576239 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: guochao <guochao@local>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:11:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Network: LinuxBridge driver - TAP + host bridge
 networking without kernel modules

Adds a driverless network backend for the KVM backend, attachable via the
generic network attachment:

  VBoxManage modifyvm <vm> --nic<N> generic --driver<N> LinuxBridge       --property<N> bridge=vboxbr0

Components:

- DrvLinuxBridge (src/VBox/Devices/Network/DrvLinuxBridge.cpp): PDM network
  transport driver. Opens /dev/net/tun and creates a non-persistent
  'vboxtapX' interface (IFF_TAP|IFF_NO_PI), then enslaves it to the
  configured host bridge via the setuid helper. Frame pump modeled on
  DrvTAP; GSO frames are carved into plain Ethernet frames.

- VBoxNetBrCtl (src/VBox/HostDrivers/adpctl/): setuid-root helper talking
  rtnetlink directly (no external tools, no shell). Restricted to
  'vboxtap*' interface names so unprivileged callers can only manipulate
  TAP devices they could create themselves. Linked statically: glibc
  ignores RUNPATH=$ORIGIN for setuid binaries (AT_SECURE), so a dynamic
  VBoxRT.so dependency would be unresolvable.

- vboxbr0-setup.sh (src/VBox/Installer/linux/): host-side one-time setup
  of the vboxbr0 bridge (static IP) plus a dnsmasq instance bound to the
  bridge only, providing DHCP (and DNS) to guests.

- VMMStatic unit-test fix: with VBOX_WITH_KVM, keep NEMR3Native-linux-x86
  in VMMStatic (APICR3/PDMR3DevMiscHlp reference the new NEMR3Kvm* entry
  points), and guard the NEMR3RunGC/NEMR3CanExecuteGuest/NEMHC*/NEMImport/
  dirty-tracking/A20 definitions with VBOX_WITH_NATIVE_NEM so the stub
  fallbacks in NEMR3.cpp/NEMAll.cpp win in the unit-test configuration,
  which filters VBOX_WITH_NATIVE_NEM out of its DEFS.

Install: VBoxNetBrCtl is installed setuid root (install.sh, chmod 4511,
root-owned). Verified end-to-end on VirtualBox 7.2.20: full build incl.
Qt GUI, setuid attach/detach smoke test against a live vboxbr0 + dnsmasq.
